{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Apples of gold</b> — that is, like forms of gold apples in settings of silver, meaning they are stored away with what is fitting for them; so too a word that is spoken on the fitting face, not to reveal another secret. Another interpretation: 'the fitting,' and not to reveal." "<b>Spoken</b> — Targum [of וינהג]: 'was led,' meaning conducted upon its face. And as a gold ring and a fine ornament, so one places reproofs upon a hearing ear." "<b>אפניו</b> — the alef is added like the alef in אפסים, אזרוע — or it is a root from אופן עגלה. And the meaning: upon its circuit and the drawing-out of hidden things and secrets. And so the interpretation [of the next verse]: do not go out hastily to join the quarrel of others, lest you be shamed."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Resolved פרוש אחר: הראויים as a shortened alternative reading of למאפיו כסף; the phrase is elliptical and possibly truncated in transmission.", 1 "The Targumic reference appears to map a form of נהג onto דבור, though the verse word is not explicitly וינהג; the connection may be to an adjacent verse or a variant tradition.", 2 "No note needed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:43.729148995Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}